    "updated_at": "2022-05-06T19:39:50Z",
    "body": "Offhand nothing else occurs to me, though you might be able to find something in the literature. If you're trying to get exactly ES Map semantics, using the same specification mechanism as ES is probably going to be easiest.\r\n\r\nSnapshotting is going to be tricky. There's a bunch of weird edge cases: like, suppose you had `[a, b, c]`, and the iterator reached and output `b`, and then while it's paused there `a` is removed and re-added - in an ES map the iterator will proceed to output `c` and then `a` again (fun!). That follows immediately from the use of tombstones but I think trying to write that down with snapshots is going to end up being pretty painful.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
